        { "text": "This is the lesson's centrepiece. Chapter 2's flattest grip, " },
        { "text": "x x 5 5 5 x", "marks": ["code"] },
        {
          "text": ", is three notes flat across one fret — three fingers in a row, or one small barre. Minor is one fret from it, and only on the top string of the three. "
