    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        { "text": "A learner who absorbed chapter 2 will expect the " },
        { "text": "B", "marks": ["code"] },
        {
          "text": " string to complicate this the way it complicated the major grid. It doesn't. The lift the "
        },
        { "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": "→" },
        { "text": "B", "marks": ["code"] },
        {
          "text": " break causes is already baked into the major grip you're comparing against — the minor move is measured against that grip, not against an all-fourths guitar built from scratch. Every set gets the same one-fret drop, this one included, and the three grips above just proved it three times over."
        }
      ]
