    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One set tested, and the rule came through untouched — a good sign that it's a fact about the third's position, not a fact that happens to be true on strings 1-2-3. Next: "
        },
        {
          "text": "the middle of the guitar",
          "link": { "kind": "article", "slug": "triad-minor-strings-3-4-5" }
        },
        {
          "text": " — the register the open C chord already lives in — where the minor move turns out to hide inside a chord you've played since your first month."
